From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 21:33:42 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: spi: apple: Add S8000 SPI
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The A9 (S8000/S8003) SPI controller has the register layout of the T8010
controller: CTRL, CFG, STATUS with the FIFO levels, PIN, TXDATA, RXDATA,
CLKDIV, the word counters and WORD_DELAY. Linux drives it with
byte-wide PIO only, so it takes no DMA channel.

Signed-off-by: Berkay Kösebay <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
[Orchard: from brkosebay/linux 28c4b7e3, 1ada4ff1 (J71t ledger 8.5); his tree had
 no binding for the separate apple,s8000-spi driver. Describe it as an
 apple,spi variant instead, without DMA.]
Co-developed-by: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Signed-off-by: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/spi/apple,spi.yaml | 12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/spi/apple,spi.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/spi/apple,spi.yaml
index ac39df7b4..b0af6b7e2 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/spi/apple,spi.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/spi/apple,spi.yaml
@@ -8,6 +8,15 @@ title: Apple ARM SoC SPI controller
 
 allOf:
   - $ref: spi-controller.yaml#
+  - if:
+      properties:
+        compatible:
+          contains:
+            const: apple,s8000-spi
+    then:
+      properties:
+        dmas: false
+        dma-names: false
 
 maintainers:
   - Hector Martin <marcan@marcan.st>
@@ -21,6 +30,7 @@ properties:
           - const: apple,t8103-spi
       - items:
           - enum:
+              - apple,s8000-spi
               - apple,t8010-spi
               - apple,t8103-spi
               - apple,t8112-spi
@@ -48,7 +58,7 @@ properties:
   apple,t8010-word-delay:
     $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint32
     description:
-      Legacy T8010 inter-word delay register value.
+      Legacy S8000/T8010 inter-word delay register value.
 
 required:
   - compatible
